## Lore

Nearly anyone can carry a card of the All Workers Political Union, the
Communist Party, and many jobs, almost every post of leadership among them,
require it. The Party runs most of civilian life and reaches into the
military as well. Commissars are its leadership: to an ordinary member what an
officer is to a private. They are held to a stricter standard than anyone
else and must follow the Party line more carefully, and the post brings both
privileges and duties. It is the main road to power for those who do not take
to military service.

Commissars are to the people what the Zampolit political officers are to the
army. They promote patriotism, loyalty and national feeling by example and by
the quiet certainty that they are watching and reporting. Some serve the
people and the Party selflessly; others are ambitious, or enjoy the little
power the job gives. Many citizens fear and distrust them, though few would
say so even in private.

## GM Notes

Commissars travel and carry goods with little hindrance, and the four Sectors
each bring their own perks; how far the immunity stretches depends on the
Sector and can be taken away as a punishment. A car or truck is a real
privilege in the Sovietski, where most people use public transport, walk or
cycle, and country folk rely on old trucks, snowmobiles and horses.
